# Rollback Rules

## Hard Rollback (action aborted fully)

- Validation failures before commit
- Permission denials
- Insufficient stock for atomic allocation when partial not chosen
- Financial invariant violations

## No Rollback of Primary Event

- Notification send failure after successful order/invoice/payment
- Analytics refresh failure
- Non-critical message delivery failure

## Compensating Actions (not silent rollback)

- Cancel remainder after partial fulfilment
- Credit note after approved return
- Payment reject after review
- Reassign delivery after staff removal

These are new official transitions, not secret undos.

---

# Partial Success Presentation Rules

When partial success occurs, user must see:

1. What succeeded (ids/counts)
2. What failed (reasons)
3. What to do next
4. Whether money/stock changed

Never show only “Success” if anything failed.

---

# Retry Safety Rules

Safe to retry freely:
- Views/searches
- Validation-fail corrections
- Connectivity fails before any acknowledgement

Retry with care / idempotent:
- Place order
- Submit payment
- Approve/reject actions
- Issue invoice
- Issue credit note

Product should prefer returning the already-created record rather than creating another.

---

# Severity & User Impact

| Severity | Examples | User expectation |
|---|---|---|
| Info denial | Filter empty | Adjust filters |
| Blocking validation | Bad qty | Fix inputs |
| Workflow blocked | Suspended / no connection | Resolve dependency |
| Financial blocked | Bad allocation | Fix settlement inputs |
| Conflict | Concurrent edit | Refresh |
| System unavailable | Connectivity | Retry later + verify critical actions |

---

# Business Impact Statements (Required Tone)

Error messages should make business impact clear:

- “Order was not created.”
- “Payment was not approved; outstanding unchanged.”
- “Inventory was not reduced.”
- “Invoice already issued; no duplicate created.”

Avoid ambiguous “Something went wrong” for known business denials.

---

# Completion Criteria

Every major failing action has known category behaviour for messaging, retry, rollback, and business impact.

